{
  "_about": "Shared cases for the graph block's spec language (20261022-064). The Python parser (app/graph_spec.py, tests/test_graph_spec.py) runs them now; the JS parser of slice 2 runs the same file. A value is a number, or the string NaN, Infinity or -Infinity: IEEE-754 doubles, and an operator or function gives what JS gives for the same doubles. Values compare with a relative tolerance of 1e-12. A rejection names the error code only: messages may differ between the two parsers, codes may not. Every name an expression needs comes from its own 'env' in this file, never from the test that runs it. A spec is split into lines on the newline character only, and its lines are numbered from 1.",

